# Build outputs
dist/
target/
# ⚠ `scripts/` was ignored here from the FIRST COMMIT (07ded32, 2026-04-08) —
# before any of the files in it existed, so it was collateral rather than a
# decision. The consequence was found on 2026-09-03: `build-release.yml` is
# tracked and invokes `scripts/build-windows.ps1`, `scripts/build-macos.sh` and
# `scripts/build-linux.sh` by name, and none of the three was in the repository.
# A CI runner clones and those steps hit "file not found", so the release
# pipeline could only ever have worked on one machine. Nothing caught it because
# no version tag has ever been pushed, so the workflow has never run.
#
# The rule is removed rather than given a fourth negation: every file in
# `scripts/` is a build orchestrator or a smoke, and both belong in version
# control. Razi-ruled 2026-09-03.

# Python
*.pyc
__pycache__/
*.pyo
*.pyd
.Python
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
ENV/
env/
build_venv/
*.egg

# Rust
target/
**/*.rs.bk
# Cargo.lock IS committed — see below. Left here as a marker so nobody
# re-adds the ignore:
#   Arcana is an application, not a library. Without a committed lockfile CI
#   resolves dependencies fresh on every run ("Locking 766 packages to latest
#   compatible versions"), so a build is not reproducible and an upstream
#   release can turn CI red with no change on our side.

# Node/NPM
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# IDE
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Tauri
src-tauri/target/

# Logs
*.log
logs/

# Environment
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# User data
.arcana/sessions/
.arcana/logs/
# Historical AutoDev local artifacts, if present in an older checkout.
.airs/sessions/
.airs/logs/

# Temporary
*.tmp
*.bak
*.cache

# Redis snapshots from the retired sidecar era must not be committed.
dump.rdb
*.rdb

# Private keys. The update-signing key is generated locally (see
# docs/updater-signing.md) and must never enter the repository.
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
# The DER intermediate the keygen runbook produces. Public half only, so not
# a leak — but it is a stray build artifact, not source.
*.der

# Stale per-member lockfiles. src-tauri and src-cli are members of the ROOT
# workspace, so cargo only ever reads /Cargo.lock; a lockfile inside a member
# is a leftover from when they were separate workspaces and is misleading.
src-tauri/Cargo.lock
src-cli/Cargo.lock
src-shared/Cargo.lock

